---
/**
 * Meet Lisa.
 *
 * Voice-forward on purpose: there is no photo of Lisa, and the trust this page
 * has to build is the trust of a phone relationship. So the page is written in
 * her voice, first person, and leans on the one number that is real and
 * verifiable — 700+ clients — rather than on invented credentials.
 *
 * The "700+ clients" figure is the only number here. No ratings, no years, no
 * carrier counts unless and until Lisa confirms them.
 */
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const title = 'Meet Lisa — Licensed Insurance Agent | Lisa’s Insurance Agency';
const description =
  'Lisa serves more than 700 clients by phone across the country — Medicare, health, dental and vision. Free help, and the same agent for the life of your policy.';

const principles = [
  {
    title: 'I work for you, not a carrier',
    copy: 'I’m a broker. No single insurance company employs me or sets my recommendations, and I represent a number of them rather than one. Where I can’t help — a company I don’t have, a plan that isn’t sold where you live — I say so and point you elsewhere.',
  },
  {
    title: 'It costs you nothing',
    copy: 'Premiums are set by the carriers and filed with regulators. You pay exactly the same whether you enroll with me, enroll on your own, or call the company directly. The carriers pay me, so my time is free to you. That’s worth saying plainly, because a lot of people assume otherwise.',
  },
  {
    title: 'I don’t disappear after you enroll',
    copy: 'The enrollment is the beginning of the relationship, not the end of it. A billing question, a rate change you don’t understand, a move to a new state, a plan that stopped covering something — you call me. Not a call centre, not a queue.',
  },
  {
    title: 'No pressure, ever',
    copy: 'I have never once needed someone to decide on the first call, and I’m not going to start. If the honest answer is that what you already have is fine, that’s the answer you’ll get.',
  },
];

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Do we have to meet in person?',
    a: 'No — and most of my clients and I never have. We handle everything by phone, and many have been with me for years. If you’d rather do it another way, tell me and we’ll work it out.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can you help in my state?',
    a: 'I’m licensed in 43 states. Ask me — if I can’t help where you are, I’ll tell you straight away rather than waste your time.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which companies do you represent?',
    a: 'A number of them, and which ones depends on the type of coverage and on where you live. I don’t represent every company available in your area, and I’ll always tell you what I can and can’t quote you. For anything outside that, Medicare.gov and 1-800-MEDICARE can show you everything.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What if I already have a plan?',
    a: 'Then the useful thing is a second opinion, and it’s free. Sometimes the review ends with me telling you to keep what you’ve got — that happens often, and it’s a perfectly good outcome.',
  },
];
---

<Page
  title={title}
  description={description}
  rawTitle
  eyebrow="Meet Lisa"
  heading="I’m Lisa. Most of my clients have never seen my face."
  intro="More than 700 people trust me with their coverage, and almost all of that relationship happens on the phone. That's not a shortcut — it's what lets me be reachable when something actually goes wrong."
>
  <!-- ─── The voice ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section" id="story" aria-labelledby="story-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">In my own words</p>

      <div class="section-intro">
        <h2 id="story-heading">What I actually do all day.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          I answer the phone. That sounds like a small thing until you’ve spent
          forty minutes in a queue trying to find out why a claim was denied.
        </p>
        <p>
          Most of my day is spent explaining things — what the difference between
          a Supplement and an Advantage plan really means, whether someone can
          delay Part B while they’re still working, why a medication that was
          covered last year isn’t this year. Some of it is enrollment paperwork.
          A good part of it is people who enrolled years ago calling with a
          problem, which is the part I’d least like to give up.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>I don’t sell over the top of people.</strong> The Medicare
          market has a reputation for exactly that, and I understand why. What I
          do instead is lay out what your options actually are, tell you what I’d
          look at in your position, and let you take as long as you need. If you
          call me back in three weeks with more questions, that’s a normal
          Tuesday.
        </p>
        <p>
          I’m licensed in 43 states, which means I can usually help wherever you
          are — and when I can’t, I say so rather than stretching to fit.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="chips">
        <span class="chip">
          <svg class="mark" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M9 16.2 4.8 12l-1.4 1.4L9 19 21 7l-1.4-1.4z"/>
          </svg>
          700+ clients
        </span>
        <span class="chip">
          <svg class="mark" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M9 16.2 4.8 12l-1.4 1.4L9 19 21 7l-1.4-1.4z"/>
          </svg>
          Licensed in 43 states
        </span>
        <span class="chip">
          <svg class="mark" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M9 16.2 4.8 12l-1.4 1.4L9 19 21 7l-1.4-1.4z"/>
          </svg>
          Free — same premium either way
        </span>
        <span class="chip">
          <svg class="mark" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M9 16.2 4.8 12l-1.4 1.4L9 19 21 7l-1.4-1.4z"/>
          </svg>
          Your agent for the life of the policy
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ─── How I work ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section section--navy" id="principles" aria-labelledby="principles-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">How I work</p>

      <div class="section-intro">
        <h2 id="principles-heading">Four things you can hold me to.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="cards cards--4">
        {principles.map((principle) => (
          <article class="card">
            <span class="check-icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor">
                <path d="M9 16.2 4.8 12l-1.4 1.4L9 19 21 7l-1.4-1.4z"/>
              </svg>
            </span>
            <h3>{principle.title}</h3>
            <p>{principle.copy}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ─── What I help with ────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section" id="what-i-help-with" aria-labelledby="help-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">What I help with</p>

      <div class="section-intro">
        <h2 id="help-heading">Three things, done properly.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          I’d rather be genuinely useful on a short list than vaguely available
          on a long one.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="cards cards--3 cards--tiles">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Medicare</h3>
          <p>Supplement, Advantage and Part D — explained in plain words, chosen with your doctors and prescriptions in front of us.</p>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/medicare">Medicare</a>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Health insurance</h3>
          <p>Marketplace coverage for individuals and families under 65, plus short-term plans for bridging a gap.</p>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/health-insurance">Health insurance</a>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Dental &amp; vision</h3>
          <p>Standalone plans you can start any time of year — on Medicare or not.</p>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/dental-insurance">Dental &amp; vision</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ─── FAQ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section section--navy" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>

      <div class="section-intro">
        <h2 id="faq-heading">Things people ask before they call.</h2>
      </div>

      <Faq items={faqs} schema />

      <div class="actions actions--stack">
        <a class="btn btn--accent" href={site.phoneHref}>Talk to Lisa · {site.phone}</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/contact">All the ways to reach me</a>
      </div>
      <p class="microline">Calling connects you with Lisa, a licensed insurance agent.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    heading="The first call is just a conversation."
    copy="No forms to fill in first, nothing to decide on the spot. Tell me where you are and we'll go from there."
  />
</Page>
